A||||5||mrfixit58||Funny Thing Happend on the way to the Post Office||||11||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||11-07-2000||01:44 PM||||The morning was around 70º and I was a little concerned about how slugglish the car felt. I had just about come to the conclusion that the motor was just acting a little cold and decided to try and wake her up by giving her about 3/4 throttle and let the RPMs wind up to about 5k. Somewhere between 3-4,000 RPMs I heard the exhaust note change and at the same time felt the car learch forward as if I flicked a NOS switch. The funny thing is... I don't have NOS. <P>After about 30-40 yards, I looked back in my rear view mirror and noticed a floating cloud on white smoke and started re-playing the sound that occured right as I heard the exhaust note change. I reminded me of the sound you get when shooting spit balls! Kind of a... THHHHUP!<P>It then occured to me what must have happened... my catalitic converter must have been partially clogging my exhaust. I know need to find a piece of stainless steel pipe to replace the cat. But, what a kick in the pants. Makes me wonder what NOS would really be like in these little cars.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||11
Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-07-2000||02:26 PM||||The fiero store carrys a "head pipe" or cat delete tube that is EASY to install.. eveyone needs nitrous in a car at least once in their life! just like Skydiving.. you gotta do it at least once!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
